# __PACKAGE_NAME__

A standalone ROHD development package using published ROHD, ROHD-HCL, and
ROHD-VF packages from pub.dev.

The starter includes two examples:

- `__MODULE_NAME__` is a small `Logic` input/output module. Its optional
  `invert` input demonstrates conditional `mux` logic and safe optional-port
  lookup with `tryInput`.
- `__MODULE_NAME__Typed` is the complex example. It demonstrates a
  `LogicStructure`, explicit-shape `LogicArray`, and `Interface` crossing a
  parent/child boundary using the public `rohd` API.

The generated source intentionally has no copyright or license header. Add the
ownership and licensing terms appropriate for your project before publishing it.

The default imports are:

```dart
import 'package:rohd/rohd.dart';
import 'package:rohd_hcl/rohd_hcl.dart';
import 'package:rohd_vf/rohd_vf.dart';
```

The generated `pubspec.yaml` uses hosted constraints by default. Re-run the
bootstrapper with `--rohd-path`, `--hcl-path`, or `--vf-path` (or their
PowerShell equivalents) to add local source overrides while developing against
unpublished framework changes.

The generated tests cover the simple conditional behavior and the complex
hierarchy, including SystemVerilog generation. Running `dart test` leaves
inspectable VCD waveforms in `tmp_test/`: `__MODULE_FILE___conditional.vcd`
for the simple optional-input example and `__MODULE_FILE___typed.vcd` for the
complex typed example. The directory is ignored by Git.

The starter follows ROHD boundary ownership rules: each constructor signal is
rebound through the matching port API, public outputs are real module ports,
and `LogicArray` ports use typed registration to preserve their complete shape.
Array outputs are driven element-by-element. The test uses `inject` for
external stimulus and reserves `put` for scheduled simulation actions.

The typed example accepts a bare packed `Logic` array source and uses
`addInputArray` and `addOutputArray` with explicit dimensions, leaf width, and
unpacked-layout metadata. A future starter revision can add a
`TypedLogicArray` example when that API is available in the hosted ROHD release.

See the [ROHD component guide](https://github.com/intel/rohd/blob/main/doc/Component.md)
for component construction and optional ROHD-HCL integration guidance. The
[ROHD hardware skill](https://github.com/intel/rohd/blob/main/.github/skills/rohd-hardware/SKILL.md)
provides additional agent guidance.

```sh
dart test
```
